          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em geometric nerve
            is a natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            operation on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tricategories"} tricategories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tricategory"} tricategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} N
                      %mo •
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{N}^{\mathsf{S}}_{\bullet}(\mathcal{C})
          %p
            Also called the
            %em Street nerve
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duskin+nerve"} Duskin nerve
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            %a{:href => "#Street1987"}
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
            = succeed "s)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oriental"} oriental
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Duskin2002"} Duskin, 2002
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#CegarraHeredia2012"} Cegarra–Heredia, 2012
          %p
            Roughly, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Street"} Street
            nerve of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            may be thought of as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} N
                    %mo •
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{N}^{\mathsf{S}}_{\bullet}(\mathcal{C})
            whose
            = succeed "-simplices" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+functors"} lax functors
            from the locally discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tricategory"} tricategory
            associated to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            satisfying a variety of unitality conditions. In detail, however, the definition is more involved, as one faces problems with the definition of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+functor"} lax functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tricategories"} tricategories
            found in (
            %a{:href => "#GPS1995"}> Gordon–Powers–Street
            ); see (
            %a{:href => "#CegarraHeredia2012"}> Definition 5.1.1 of Cegarra–Heredia
            ).
          %p
            There are other nerve constructions for tricategories besides the Street nerve. One of them is the
            = succeed "," do
              %strong Grothendieck nerve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tricategory"} tricategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            associates a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudosimplicial+bicategory"}> pseudosimplicial bicategory
            ”
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} N
                      %mo •
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Bicats
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{N}^\mathsf{G}_\bullet(\mathcal{C})\colon\Delta^\op\longrightarrow\mathsf{Bicats}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^\op
            to the tricategory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Bicats
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Bicats}
            = succeed "-simplices" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-tuples" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            One also has the
            %strong Segal nerve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} N
                    %mo •
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Segal
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Bicats
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{N}^\mathsf{Segal}_\bullet(\mathcal{C})\colon\Delta^\op\longrightarrow\mathsf{Bicats}
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} N
                      %mo •
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{N}^\mathsf{G}_\bullet(\mathcal{C})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is the locally discrete tricategory associated to a bicategory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            agrees with the
            = succeed "-nerve" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            introduced in (
            %a{:href => "#LackPaoli2006"}> Lack–Paoli, 2006
            ).
          %p
            All of these nerve constructions are equivalent in the sense that their classifying spaces are homotopy equivalent to each other. For more details, see (
            %a{:href => "#CegarraHeredia2012"}> Cegarra–Heredia, 2012
            ).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              The Street nerve identifies precisely nerves of
              = succeed "s" do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  trigroupoid
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/trigroupoid"} ?
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
              = succeed "s:" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypergroupoid"} hypergroupoid
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
              for which the horn fillers in dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq 4
              are
              = succeed ";" do
                %em unique
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Carrasco2014"} Carrasco, 2014
          %h2#picturing_the_street_nerve Picturing the Street nerve
